[128.933036, "o", "    'The parameterized `analyze` function applies geography, race coding, outcome and hit definitions, time adjustments, and inference choices from `selections`. Unadjusted universes use race-group proportion differences. Adjusted universes use logistic regression with age, sex, stop-reason, and selected time controls; officer-clustered covariance is used for clustered specifications. Estimates are standardized by the sample SD of the focal race indicator. Search-and-hit universes combine the two outcome estimates by inverse-variance weighting.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.93306, "o", "    if vals:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.933478, "o", "        lines += ['',f'Standardized estimates range from {min(vals):.5g} to {max(vals):.5g}; median {np.median(vals):.5g}. Positive values indicate a higher outcome for the focal black/non-white comparison relative to white.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.933792, "o", "        for k in ['geographic_scope','race_comparison_set','bias_outcome','hit_definition','time_of_day_adjustment','outcome_model_and_inference']:\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h>             groups={}\r\n"]
[128.933828, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.934065, "o", "            for r in good: groups.setdefault(r['decisions'].get(k),[]).append(r['estimate_standardized'])\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.934197, "o", "            spans=[max(v)-min(v) for v in groups.values() if len(v)>1]\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.934437, "o", "            lines.append(f'- {k}: maximum within-option spread {max(spans) if spans else 0:.5g}')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.934652, "o", "    lines += ['', 'Failed or unidentified fits retain null statistics and `converged: false`; no verdict field is emitted.']\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[128.934809, "o", "    with open('/app/results.md','w') as f: f.write('\\n'.join(lines)+'\\n')\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
